---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../data/site';

const effectiveDate = '9 August 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy — GoServe"
  description="How GoServe collects, uses, and protects data for cafe staff and owners using our POS, kitchen display, and inventory software."
>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy policy" lede={`Effective date: ${effectiveDate}`} />

  <section class="legal-section">
    <div class="container narrow prose">
      <p>
        GoServe (&ldquo;GoServe&rdquo;, &ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;) provides point-of-sale, kitchen
        display, and inventory software for cafes and restaurants (&ldquo;Workspaces&rdquo;) in Nepal, through
        our web app, the Go Serve mobile app, and our API. This policy explains what we collect from the
        people who use those products &mdash; primarily cafe staff and owners &mdash; and how we handle it.
      </p>
      <p>
        This app is a business tool. It is provisioned by a Workspace owner for their staff; there is no
        public sign-up or consumer account creation inside the app itself.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Account information.</strong> When you sign in &mdash; by email one-time passcode or by
        &ldquo;Continue with Google&rdquo; &mdash; we collect your email address, and, if you use Google
        Sign-In, your name and profile photo as provided by Google. We do not receive or store your Google
        password.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Workspace and operational data.</strong> Once signed in, the data you create or view through
        the app &mdash; orders, tabs, menu items, inventory counts, receipts, staff records, and reports
        &mdash; is stored against your Workspace. This data belongs to the Workspace (your employer/business),
        not to you individually.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Photos.</strong> If you attach a photo to a menu item, a staff profile, or a receipt using the
        app&rsquo;s camera/photo-library picker, that image is uploaded to our storage backend and associated
        with that record.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Device and diagnostic information.</strong> We do not use any third-party analytics or
        crash-reporting service in the mobile app. Our backend logs standard server-side request metadata
        (e.g. timestamps, IP address, error traces) for security and reliability, in line with normal
        web-service operation.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>What we do not collect.</strong> We do not collect your device&rsquo;s precise location. We do
        not access your contacts, calendar, or SMS. We do not serve ads and do not use any advertising SDK.
      </p>

      <h2>Payments</h2>
      <p>
        Digital wallet payments (eSewa, Khalti) are completed through those providers&rsquo; own QR-based
        payment flow at the point of sale &mdash; the Go Serve app does not process, transmit, or store your
        card or wallet credentials. Card/cash transaction records kept in the app (amounts, tender type, VAT)
        are the Workspace&rsquo;s business records, not personal financial instruments you&rsquo;ve given us.
      </p>

      <h2>How we use what we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To authenticate you and keep you signed in.</li>
        <li>To operate the core product: orders, kitchen tickets, inventory, billing, and reporting for your Workspace.</li>
        <li>To provide customer support when you contact us.</li>
        <li>To maintain security (e.g. detecting abuse, rate-limiting).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not sell personal information, and we do not share it with third-party advertisers, data
        brokers, or analytics companies. We do not use your data to train third-party AI models.
      </p>

      <h2>Where data is stored and how it&rsquo;s protected</h2>
      <p>
        Your data is stored in our own backend infrastructure (database and file storage that we operate or
        contract directly, not resold to other companies). All traffic between the app and our servers is
        encrypted in transit (HTTPS/TLS and WSS). On your device, a small amount of data is kept locally so
        the app keeps working offline &mdash; cached menu/order data and a queue of not-yet-synced actions, and
        your signed-in session token (via the device&rsquo;s secure credential storage) &mdash; this local copy
        is cleared when you sign out or uninstall the app.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can review and update your name/email in the app&rsquo;s account settings. You can ask us to
        export a copy of the personal data we hold about you, or to delete your account, by emailing{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, or via the Settings page in the GoServe web
        app if your Workspace owner has given you access. Account deletion revokes your access and anonymizes
        your personal identifiers; records that belong to the Workspace (orders, audit history) are retained
        by the Workspace, since they are the business&rsquo;s operating records, not yours individually. If you
        are the sole owner of a Workspace, you&rsquo;ll need to transfer ownership or close the Workspace before
        your personal account can be deleted.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        GoServe is a business tool for cafe staff and owners. It is not directed at children, and we do not
        knowingly collect data from anyone under 16.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We&rsquo;ll update the effective date above when this policy changes, and post material changes here
        before they take effect.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal-section {
    padding-block: clamp(16px, 3vw, 40px) clamp(56px, 8vw, 96px);
  }
</style>
